# T7b re-review 1: a recorded clip starts exactly on the close boundary, not a 16th late. The
# transport starts at REC (step 0); REC closes at the next bar so rec.close = 32 (a 2-bar take); the
# clip starts at step 32 and its progress at step 48 is 16/32 = 128/256.
wait 300
cursor 1 0
tap REC
expect recrec 1
wait-bar 1
expect globalstep 16
tap REC
wait-bar 1
expect globalstep 32
expect liveclip1 7
expect liveprog1 0
wait-bar 1
expect globalstep 48
expect liveprog1 128
wait 1400
shot studio_cliprec_at.png
dump studio_cliprec_at.json
